Package: codehover
Type: Package
Title: Hoverable HTML Tables That Reveal ggplot Code Step by Step
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Arthur", "Welle", email = "arthurwelle@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Creates interactive HTML tables where each row is a step of
    code and hovering a row shows the corresponding image. The main entry
    point ch_hover() takes ggplot code, splits it automatically at every
    top-level '+', renders one image per step and returns a self-contained
    HTML object (CSS and JavaScript included) that works in R Markdown,
    Quarto and the RStudio viewer. Rows also respond to tap and keyboard
    navigation. A low-level API (ch_int(), ch_row(), ch_out()) remains
    available for hand-built tables with arbitrary images and pseudo-code.
